---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "@/components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Theming"
  description="Tokens, layers, the color scheme and the public style contract."
>
  <div class="docs-content">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow">Getting started</p>
    <h1>Theming</h1>
    <p class="docs-lead">
      Components read semantic CSS custom properties. Override tokens to change the look
      without editing component CSS. Geometry and spacing come from a style; see
      <a href="/docs/styles">Styles</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Layers</h2>
    <p>
      The generated <code>index.css</code> declares the layer order. Keep it before your own
      layers so component styles can be overridden deliberately.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      code={`@layer loseta.tokens, loseta.reset, loseta.base, loseta.components, loseta.style, loseta.utilities;`}
    />

    <h2>Token convention</h2>
    <p>
      Most tokens come in pairs: a surface and the foreground that sits on it. The surface
      token has no suffix; its text and icon color adds <code>-foreground</code>.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      code={`:root {
  --primary: oklch(0.205 0 0);
  --primary-foreground: oklch(0.985 0 0);
}`}
    />
    <p>
      A component that sets <code>background-color: var(--primary)</code> pairs it with
      <code>color: var(--primary-foreground)</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Color roles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>--background</code> / <code>--foreground</code> — page surface and primary text.
      </li>
      <li><code>--card</code> / <code>--card-foreground</code> — cards and alerts.</li>
      <li>
        <code>--popover</code> / <code>--popover-foreground</code> — dialogs, popovers, menus
        and tooltips.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>--primary</code> / <code>--primary-foreground</code> — primary actions and
        checked controls.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>--secondary</code> / <code>--secondary-foreground</code> — secondary actions and
        badges.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>--muted</code> / <code>--muted-foreground</code> — subdued surfaces,
        descriptions and secondary text.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>--accent</code> / <code>--accent-foreground</code> — highlighted and focused
        menu items.
      </li>
      <li><code>--destructive</code> — destructive actions, invalid borders and invalid text.</li>
      <li><code>--border</code> — separators, outlines and outline-variant borders.</li>
      <li><code>--input</code> — form-control borders and subtle control fills in dark mode.</li>
      <li><code>--ring</code> — focus border and focus shadow.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <code>--chart-*</code>, <code>--sidebar-*</code> and <code>--scrollbar-*</code> are
      reserved families shipped with the style; v1 components do not consume them.
    </p>

    <h2>Radius</h2>
    <p>
      <code>--radius</code> is the base value; the scale multiplies it. Styles may cap the
      radius of small controls so they stay visually consistent.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>--radius-sm</code>: <code>0.6 × --radius</code>.</li>
      <li><code>--radius-md</code>: <code>0.8 × --radius</code>.</li>
      <li><code>--radius-lg</code>: <code>--radius</code>.</li>
      <li><code>--radius-xl</code>: <code>1.4 × --radius</code>.</li>
      <li>
        <code>--radius-2xl</code> to <code>--radius-4xl</code>: <code>1.8 ×</code> to
        <code>2.6 × --radius</code>.
      </li>
      <li><code>--radius-full</code>: fully rounded.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Adding tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Define a new token under <code>:root</code> and <code>.dark</code>, then use it from the
      files you own.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      code={`:root {
  --warning: oklch(0.84 0.16 84);
  --warning-foreground: oklch(0.28 0.07 46);
}

.dark {
  --warning: oklch(0.41 0.11 46);
  --warning-foreground: oklch(0.99 0.02 95);
}`}
    />

    <h2>Dark mode</h2>
    <p>
      Add <code>.dark</code> to the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element. The token file also sets
      <code>color-scheme</code> so native controls follow the color scheme.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock lang="js" code={`document.documentElement.classList.toggle("dark", isDark);`} />

    <h2>Styles</h2>
    <p>
      Nova is the default style. A style changes geometry, spacing, control sizes, radii and
      the type scale; it does not change tokens or markup. <a href="/docs/styles">Styles</a>
      lists every shipped style and how to switch.
    </p>

    <h2>Public style contract</h2>
    <p>
      Components expose variants, sizes and states through data attributes and ARIA. The most
      common hooks are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>data-variant</code> and <code>data-size</code> for visual variants.</li>
      <li><code>data-slot="title|description|action|header|shortcut|indicator"</code> for parts.</li>
      <li><code>aria-invalid="true"</code> for invalid controls.</li>
      <li><code>aria-selected="true"</code> for tabs, options and selectable rows.</li>
      <li><code>aria-checked="true"</code> for checkable menu items.</li>
      <li><code>data-highlighted</code> for the highlighted menu item.</li>
      <li><code>:disabled</code> and <code>aria-disabled="true"</code> for disabled states.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="docs-callout">
      <strong>No prefixes.</strong> Classes and tokens are intentionally unprefixed to match
      shadcn/ui and the source nomenclature. Use one design system per project to avoid
      collisions.
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
